  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 63.9% accuracy, giving us a baseline but no information about which image encoder is superior. Uncertainty: The image encoder is a critical design choice—ResNet50 (~25M params) vs. ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L (~300M params) represent a large capacity gap, and we don't know whether the stronger image features translate to better multimodal fusion performance. This experiment (config_006) changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings identical to config_001, making it a clean single-variable ablation. Rationale: With 8 experiments remaining, establishing whether the image encoder is a major lever early will guide the bulk of subsequent experiments. If ViT-L substantially improves accuracy, we can focus the remaining budget on optimizing around it (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion); if not, we save experiments by not exploring that branch. This is the highest-information single experiment available given the sparse evidence."
}

